# UI Rules

## Structure

- Import alias: `@/` → `src/` (Vite).
- Pages: `src/pages/{domain}/{listing|detail}/` with `blocks/` subcomponents and barrel `index.js`.
- Shell: Metronic demo1 layout (`src/layouts/demo1/`) — sidebar, header, content area.
- Product pages live under `src/pages/`, not Metronic demo copies.

## Components

- Shadcn primitives in `@/components/ui/*` (`button`, `input`, `dialog`, etc.) — reuse before raw HTML.
- Lists: `DataGrid*` components + React Query (providers in `ProvidersWrapper.jsx`).
- Toasts: `sonner` (`toast.error`, `toast.success`).
- Motion: `@/motion` (`RouteTransitionProvider`, skeletons for loading states).
- Auth loading: `ScreenLoader` during bootstrap.

## Routing & access

- Wrap protected routes in `RequireAuth`.
- Feature gates: `<RoleRoute section={SECTIONS.X}>` using `roleAccess.js`.
- New sections: add to `@/constants/portalSections` and path rules in `roleAccess.js`.

## API calls in pages

- Use `import.meta.env.VITE_APP_API_URL` with axios (via global `setupAxios`).
- Show user-facing errors from `error.response.data.message`.
- Shared helpers: `showTaskApiError`, `getTaskApiErrorMessage` pattern for consistent UX.

## Do's

- Follow existing page/block folder conventions when adding features.
- Use theme tokens (`--ax-*`, Shadcn vars) — `theme-rules.mdc` is globally enforced.
- Keep provider order consistent in `ProvidersWrapper.jsx`.

## Don'ts

- Don't add routes without `RequireAuth` / `RoleRoute` where applicable.
- Don't import Metronic demo pages as product code.
- Don't hardcode colors — use design tokens.
